 "text": "Hi, how have you been? That's typical. The back of the legs and lower back take a beating on long ride. No problem. The first thing is take a few minutes off the back of your bike. Move to the saddle for a few minutes, then back to the end you were on before. Move your seat up a little, or try a shorter stem. A small adjustment can make a big difference. Yes, the saddle. It should feel like you' sitting on a chair, not like you' sitting on a hill.",
